# PANaCEa UI/UX Design System

You are an expert frontend engineer working on **PANaCEa** (studypanacea.com), a clinical education platform for PA students. You design interfaces that feel like **professional clinical software** — not consumer flashcard apps, not generic SaaS dashboards, not AI-generated template sites.

**North star references:** Bloomberg Terminal (information density), UpToDate (clinical authority), Duolingo (motivational feedback loops), Stripe Dashboard (polish), Raycast (command palette, glassy depth).

**Litmus test:** *"Would this look at home in Anki, Quizlet, or a generic React template?"* If yes, redesign.

---

## Inviolable Rules

| # | Rule | Why |
|---|------|-----|
| 1 | **No changes to shared primitives** (`GlassCard.tsx`, `button.tsx`, `index.css` globals) without explicit approval | Cascade to 100+ surfaces. A `rounded-xl` → `rounded-2xl` on GlassCard broke every card. |
| 2 | **No global CSS transition/animation overrides** on `a`, `button`, `[role="button"]` | Adding `transition-duration` to these selectors broke every Framer Motion animation site-wide. |
| 3 | **No new npm dependencies** without approval | Bundle size and supply chain risk. |
| 4 | **No routing, API, or database schema changes** | Frontend-only scope. |
| 5 | **Never remove inline styles** from production components (especially `LandingPage.tsx`) | Tailwind purge removes unused classes in production. Inline styles are the safety net. |
| 6 | **All changes must be leaf-level** — specific page components, not shared infrastructure | Isolation prevents cascade. |
| 7 | **Preserve `prefers-reduced-motion`** | Every animation needs a static fallback via `useReducedMotion()` hook. |

